WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.530
Francis of Assisi heard
Jesus' words about wealth,

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.110
and gave away everything he had.

3
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.480
Centuries later, John
Wesley told Christians:

4
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:13.880
gain all you can, save all
you can, give all you can.

5
00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.260
Both were reading the same Gospel.

6
00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:20.260
In Luke, Jesus says: Blessed
are you who are poor.

7
00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.420
So did Jesus really mean that literally?

8
00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:26.630
In this mission, you'll
read his blessings and woes,

9
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.190
and his command to love your enemies.

10
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.510
Then you'll compare how
Christians live these words today,

11
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.330
from vows of poverty to stewardship.

12
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:40.050
Your mission: weigh up whether Jesus
meant his blessing on the poor literally.
